  "title": "Consciousness attribution, process-based or state-based",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "576b7538-39eb-4bdf-8653-cba6bea0d621",
      "text": "A consciousness attribution assigns a consciousness state $C_t$ (binary, graded or structured) to a bounded system at time $t$ as $C_t = f(X_t, X_{<t})$. It is process-based when it depends on the prior local history $X_{<t}$ and state-based when $C_t = f(X_t)$.",
